## warcraft2.yaml

faction_wc2_humans =
   .description = Humans from Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness
      Leaders of the Alliance. Mighty and intelligent. The Humans of Warcraft 2
      represent the kingdoms of Azeroth, Lordaeron, and their allies, fighting
      against the orcish Horde with knights, mages, paladins, and elven archers.
      Their society is built on honor, faith, and arcane magic, drawing power
      from the Holy Light and the arcane traditions of Dalaran.

      In Cameo, the Humans are a balanced faction with strong magic, naval
      capabilities, and versatile infantry. Their economy uses three resources
      (Gold, Wood, Oil) instead of the standard ore/Tiberium system. The Church
      provides Holy Vision (map reveal) and Healing support powers, while Mages
      cast devastating Blizzard spells. The Paladin is their signature unit —
      a holy warrior with healing and exorcism abilities.

      Difficulty: ©©©
      Early Game: ©©©
      Mid Game: ©©©©
      Late Game: ©©©©
      Playstyle: Balanced / Magic / Naval
      Strength: Paladins, Mages, Knights, Elven Archers, Naval Dominance
      Weakness: Fragile Basic Infantry, Reliance on Upgrades
      Countered by: Swarm Tactics, Fast Rushes, Air Power

      Special Units: Paladin (holy warrior with healing), Mage (Blizzard,
        Polymorph, Flame Strike), Knight (fast heavy cavalry), Elven Archer/Ranger,
        Footman, Gnomish Flying Machine, Gryphon Rider, Dwarven Demolition Squad
      Special Buildings: Church (Holy Vision, Healing), Mage Tower,
        Gryphon Aviary, Shipyard, Elven Lumber Mill, Stables
      Team Upgrades: Sword upgrades, Armor upgrades, Mage spell research,
        Archer marksmanship, Knight speed
      Support powers: Holy Vision, Healing
      Superweapons: Blizzard (via Church/IonCannonPower)

      Features:
      - Three-resource economy: Gold, Wood, Oil
      - Paladin: holy warrior with Healing and Exorcism abilities
      - Mage: casts Blizzard (area damage), Polymorph (transforms enemy),
        Flame Strike
      - Knight: fast heavy cavalry for flanking and raiding
      - Elven Archer/Ranger: versatile ranged infantry with upgrade potential
      - Gnomish Flying Machine: scout for vision
      - Gryphon Rider: powerful flying unit
      - Dwarven Demolition Squad: explosive anti-building infantry
      - Shipyard and naval units: Transport, Destroyer, Battleship
      - Church provides Holy Vision (map reveal) and Healing support powers
      - Blizzard superweapon: devastating area-of-effect spell

faction_wc2_orcs =
   .description = Orcs from Warcraft II: Tides of Darkness
      Leaders of the Horde. Brutish and crafty. The Orcs of Warcraft 2 are the
      invading Horde from Draenor, fighting with ogres, death knights, berserkers,
      and troll axethrowers. Their magic is darker and more destructive than the
      Humans', drawing on necromancy and demonic power. The Horde values raw
      strength and aggression over defense and subtlety.

      In Cameo, the Orcs are an aggressive faction with powerful dark magic and
      strong melee units. Their economy mirrors the Humans (Gold, Wood, Oil).
      The Temple provides Eye of Kilrogg (scouting) and Runes (trap) support
      powers, while Death Knights cast devastating Death and Decay. The Ogre-Mage
      is their signature unit — a brutal melee fighter with Bloodlust buffs and
      Runes traps. The Horde excels at aggressive pushes and area denial.

      Difficulty: ©©©
      Early Game: ©©©©
      Mid Game: ©©©
      Late Game: ©©©©
      Playstyle: Aggressive / Dark Magic / Naval
      Strength: Ogre-Magi, Death Knights, Berserkers, Bloodlust Buffs
      Weakness: Fragile Ranged Units, Reliance on Melee
      Countered by: Positional Defense, Air Power, Mage Spells

      Special Units: Ogre-Mage (heavy melee with Bloodlust and Runes),
        Death Knight (Death and Decay, Haste, Raise Dead), Berserker,
        Troll Axethrower, Grunt, Goblin Zeppelin, Dragon, Goblin Sappers
      Special Buildings: Temple (Eye of Kilrogg, Runes), Altar of Storms,
        Dragon Roost, Shipyard, Troll Lumber Mill, Ogre Mound
      Team Upgrades: Axe upgrades, Armor upgrades, Death Knight spell research,
        Berserker strength, Ogre-Mage spells (Bloodlust, Runes)
      Support powers: Eye of Kilrogg, Runes
      Superweapons: Death and Decay (via Temple/IonCannonPower)

      Features:
      - Three-resource economy: Gold, Wood, Oil
      - Ogre-Mage: heavy melee with Bloodlust (buff) and Runes (trap)
      - Death Knight: casts Death and Decay (area damage), Haste, Raise Dead
      - Berserker: upgraded ranged infantry with enhanced combat stats
      - Troll Axethrower: basic ranged infantry
      - Goblin Zeppelin: scout/transport for aerial vision
      - Dragon: powerful flying unit
      - Goblin Sappers: explosive anti-building infantry
      - Shipyard and naval units: Transport, Destroyer, Juggernaut
      - Temple provides Eye of Kilrogg (scouting) and Runes (trap) support powers
      - Death and Decay superweapon: devastating expanding area-of-effect spell
      - Bloodlust: team buff that dramatically increases melee damage

